<title>GERMANY: Mitsuzuka says yen's downward correction completed.</title>
<headline>Mitsuzuka says yen's downward correction completed.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Saturday the yen's downward correction since April 1995 has been completed.</p>
<p>He also told reporters at the end of meeting of Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers and central bank leaders that an overly strong or weak yen was unfavourable.</p>
<p>In addition, Mitsuzuka said Japan was pleased the G7 statement issued after the meeting in Berlin included Japan's views on currency markets.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
